1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,425
Daily sales jump up and down like waves on the sea. A moving average looks at the tide, not the waves.

2
00:00:09,130 --> 00:00:16,630
December always beats March. Compare December with last December, so the season cancels out.

3
00:00:18,330 --> 00:00:28,030
Three days of sales: ten, fourteen and twelve. The three-day average is twelve. Next day, drop the oldest and add the newest.

4
00:00:28,730 --> 00:00:33,205
The line becomes smooth, and the real trend shows through.

5
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:41,675
Sales up twenty percent in a year of twenty-five percent inflation means real sales fell.

6
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:48,355
And a fall of fifty percent needs a rise of one hundred percent to recover.

